This repository is not under a single license. Every file declares its own with
an SPDX header, following the REUSE specification (https://reuse.software/);
full texts are in LICENSES/.

    flydigi/, tools/, tests/          MIT
      except the Qt-dependent files: tools/generate-qmltypes, tests/test_models.py,
      tests/test_qml.py, tests/test_shell.py, tests/qml_harness.py, tests/qml/
                                      GPL-3.0-or-later
    README.md, PROGRESS.md, docs/     MIT
    PROTOCOL.md                       CC0-1.0
    udev/, pipewire/, .gitignore      CC0-1.0
    gui/                              GPL-3.0-or-later

The split is deliberate. The protocol implementation is MIT because I have no
objection to anyone reusing it, in any project, under any license. PROTOCOL.md
and the system configuration files are public domain because protocol facts and
copy-pasteable config should carry no attribution burden at all.

Copyleft is confined to what links Qt: gui/, and the Qt-dependent files under
tools/ and tests/ listed above. Nobody needs to embed those, so GPL costs
nothing there.

MIT is one-way compatible with GPL: the GUI importing flydigi/ does not make
flydigi/ GPL, and those files remain independently reusable.

A binary release that bundles the GUI is conveyed as a whole under GPL-3.0
terms. That is expected -- see README.md, "Building a release".

flydigi/ps5_data.py is generated from inputtino and is additionally copyright
Games on Whales under the MIT License; see NOTICE.

Run `reuse lint` to verify any of this.
